      "summary": "The Terraform precondition normalizes principal IDs, but the regression test does not exercise the case-only match required by AC RELEASE-ID-03.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/release-identity.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 459,
          "message": "AC RELEASE-ID-03 requires a regression test for a case-only GUID match. Use mocked principal IDs containing letters and set terraform_principal_object_id to a casing variant; assert that the precondition rejects it.",
          "confidence": 0.98,
          "category": "other",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The federated_identities_are_distinct_principals run sets the workflow principal IDs and terraform_principal_object_id to numeric-only GUIDs. Its inequality assertion therefore cannot distinguish a case-insensitive precondition from a case-sensitive one.",
            "failureScenario": "If the main.tf precondition regresses to case-sensitive comparisons, this test still passes because the configured input differs from both mocked principals and none contains letters whose casing could vary. A case-only match could then allow the Contributor grant to target a workflow identity, contrary to AC RELEASE-ID-03."
          }
        }
